    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1369">

                <pb facs="1625" n="1427" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1427"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119/7–545</note>
                <head>No. 1369<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Proposal by the Soviet
                        Delegation</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1369-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation?]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">The Black Sea Straits</hi></p>
                <p rendition="#center">(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Soviet Proposal</hi>)</p>
                <p>With regard to the regime of the Black Sea Straits, the Conference found
                    necessary that:</p>
                <p>1. The International Straits Convention signed in Montreux shall be abrogated in
                    the proper regular procedure as it no longer corresponds to the present time
                    conditions.</p>
                <p>2. The determination of the regime of the Straits—the only sea passage from and
                    to the Black Sea—shall fall within the province of Turkey and the Soviet Union
                    as the states chiefly concerned and capable of ensuring the freedom of
                    commercial navigation and the security in the Black Sea Straits.</p>
                <p>3. In addition to other measures the new Straits regime should also provide for
                    the following:</p>
                <p>In the interests of their own security and maintenance of peace in the area of
                    [the] Black Sea[,] Turkey and the Soviet Union shall prevent by their common
                    facilities in the Straits the use of the Straits by <pb facs="1626" n="1428"
                        xml:id="pg1428"/> the other countries for the purposes inimical to the Black
                    Sea powers (in addition to Turkish military bases the establishment of Soviet
                    military bases in the Straits).</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Babelsberg</hi></placeName>], <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-22">7/22/45</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1369-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1369-f1-content">
                <p>This question was raised at the Sixth Plenary Meeting, July 22. See <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg256">p. 256</ref>. For the
                    draft entry on this subject submitted by the Soviet Delegation for inclusion in
                    the Protocol, see <ref target="#d1433">document No. 1433</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
